# Trivy vulnerability-ignore list.
#
# Every entry here is a documented decision that a specific CVE/advisory does
# not apply to this project. Suppression is not exemption — when the
# underlying dependency is upgraded past these, remove the entry and confirm
# with a fresh scan.
#
# Migrated from .owasp/dependency-check-suppressions.xml when CI moved from
# OWASP dependency-check to Trivy — see .github/workflows/trivy-scan.yml for
# why.

# ── swagger-ui bundled DOMPurify (client-side JavaScript) ───────────────────
# DOMPurify is a browser-only DOM sanitizer, bundled inside swagger-ui's JS
# files. It executes in the user's browser when a developer opens
# /swagger-ui.html locally to explore the API; it never runs server-side.
# These advisories describe XSS vectors triggered by malicious HTML input in
# a browser session — a threat model with no analog here (we don't accept or
# render untrusted HTML anywhere in the app). Removing swagger-ui to satisfy
# the scanner would drop the interactive API docs, which are the primary
# integrator on-ramp; the risk/benefit does not favor that.
#
# Revisit if swagger-ui ships an updated DOMPurify (currently blocked by
# swagger-ui's own release cadence, tracked in swagger-api/swagger-ui).
